WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.750
Time a falling ball with a stopwatch.

2
00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:04.310
Then do it again.

3
00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:05.480
And again.

4
00:00:05.530 --> 00:00:07.890
0.62 seconds.

5
00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:09.710
0.57.

6
00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:11.500
0.65.

7
00:00:11.550 --> 00:00:13.530
0.60.

8
00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:15.340
Never quite the same.

9
00:00:15.390 --> 00:00:16.950
Readings scatter.

10
00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:20.350
So when a set of readings
agrees almost perfectly,

11
00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:22.100
it feels like proof.

12
00:00:22.150 --> 00:00:26.640
But can readings agree perfectly with
each other and still all be wrong?

13
00:00:26.690 --> 00:00:30.260
In this mission, you'll find
where an uncertainty comes from:

14
00:00:30.310 --> 00:00:34.370
a scale, a digital display,
or a set of repeats.

15
00:00:34.420 --> 00:00:39.250
Then you'll judge results properly, and
learn why 'be more careful' is never an

16
00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:40.490
improvement.

17
00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:44.560
Your mission: decide whether
agreeing readings can all be wrong,

18
00:00:44.610 --> 00:00:45.790
and explain why.
